# ── never commit these ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A signing key in git history is a signing key you have to replace, and Play
# App Signing will not let you replace an upload key without a support round
# trip. Treat any accidental commit of these as a key compromise.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
key.properties
google-services.json
*.p8
*.p12
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Razorpay Key Secret, Play service-account JSON, and anything else with a
# credential in it. Named explicitly so the intent survives a refactor.
**/secrets/
*service-account*.json

# ── node ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
.vite/
*.local

# ── capacitor / android ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
android/app/build/
android/build/
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
android/app/release/
android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/
*.apk
*.aab
.gradle/
captures/

# ── editor / os ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── build artefacts of the single-file builds ─────────────────────────────
aliquot-offline.html
aliquot-preview.html
*.zip
